{"type": "tool_call", "n": 16, "ts": 1790156113.643001, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "DE \u2014 March 2026 Cutoff & JE Review Memo\n\nScope: Reviewed all 28 DE ledger entries posted in March 2026 (period 2026-03) for cutoff accuracy and adequacy of support, cross-checking against underlying vendor bills/invoices and adjacent-period activity (Feb/Apr).\n\nFindings & Actions Taken:\n\n1. CUTOFF ERROR \u2014 CORRECTED\n   JE-00305 \"Nordwolke Hosting - NW-2026-0402 - dedicated cluster\" (\u20ac5,600.00; Dr 5000 Hosting & Infrastructure / Cr 2000 AP), dated 2026-03-31.\n   - Supporting invoice DOC-0206 is dated 2026-04-02 with an explicit service period of 2026-04-01 to 2026-04-30 (April dedicated cluster charge). This is an April expense that was booked into March in error.\n   - Action: Reversed JE-00305 in March via JE-00306 (dated 2026-03-31, same support DOC-0206), removing the \u20ac5,600 expense/AP liability from the March period.\n   - Note: April (2026-04) is not yet an open posting period, so the correct-period entry (Dr 5000 / Cr 2000, \u20ac5,600, dated 2026-04-02, support DOC-0206) could not be posted today. This should be booked as part of April processing once that period opens \u2014 flagging here for AP follow-up so it isn't missed.\n\n2. UNSUPPORTED ENTRY \u2014 ESCALATED (EXC-001)\n   JE-00298 \"Umsatzkorrektur Q1\" (\u20ac9,999.00; Dr 1100 AR / Cr 4000 Subscription Revenue), dated 2026-03-29, posted manually by m.krause, no supporting documentation attached and none found in the document store despite search. The generic memo, lack of invoice/contract backup, and round dollar amount are additional red flags.\n   - Action: Flagged as exception (EXC-001) for controller review with the preparer rather than force a reconciliation. Recommend excluding this \u20ac9,999 from March DE revenue until substantiated, and reversing if support cannot be produced before lock.\n\n3. ALL OTHER MARCH DE ACTIVITY \u2014 NO ISSUES\n   Remaining 26 entries (recurring AR subscription invoices/receipts for Kessler AG, Vogel Logistik, Brandt Maschinenbau; recurring AP bills/payments for rent, hosting, software, utilities, marketing; card/travel expenses; two payroll runs and funding transfers) were all dated within their correct service/payment periods and are supported. No further cutoff issues identified.\n\nChecklist: \"AP cutoff review\" (DE) marked complete. Remaining open DE checklist items (bank reconciliations, depreciation, prepaid software amortization, payroll accrual, revenue recognition, intercompany reconciliation, flux review) are outside the scope of this cutoff/JE review and remain open for their respective owners.\n\nNet impact of corrections: March DE expense reduced by \u20ac5,600 (Hosting & Infrastructure) and AP reduced by \u20ac5,600, pending controller resolution of the \u20ac9,999 unsupported revenue item (EXC-001)."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 7}
